Description: OpenTelemetry Python Proto definitions
 OpenTelemetry is a collection of tools, APIs, and SDKs used to instrument,
 generate, collect, and export telemetry data (metrics, logs, and traces).
 .
 This package provides the generated Protocol Buffer bindings for the
 OTLP wire format, shared by the OTLP gRPC and HTTP exporters.
 .
 This package supersedes Debian's own python3-opentelemetry-proto
 (1.5.0-1), which tracks an old, pre-monorepo standalone versioning
 scheme for the OTLP proto definitions and is far behind what current
 opentelemetry-sdk/-exporter-otlp-* releases expect. Verified compatible
 at runtime with Debian trixie's python3-protobuf (3.21.12): the
 upstream pyproject.toml's "protobuf>=5.0,<7.0" constraint is a
 conservative pip-metadata pin, not an actual generated-code
 requirement -- smoke-tested importing, serializing and parsing
 trace/metrics OTLP messages against protobuf 3.21.12 succeeds.
 .
 This package provides the Python 3 library.
